WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.970
SPEAKER: Vision API can be
used to extract information

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:07.890
from images, such as labels,
text, landmarks, and more.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.860
Let's see how to use
Vision API with C#.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.430
First, make sure Vision API
is enabled in your project

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.460
and a service account
exists to make API calls.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.410
Both are explained in the
code lab in the video notes.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:27.600
In Cloud Shell, let's create a
simple .NET console app and add

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.290
Vision API Nougat
package to the project.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:36.990
Open the online code editor
and navigate to program.cs.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.770
We will perform text
detection on this image.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.710
First, reference
Vision API library

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.250
and create an image
annotator client.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:52.910
Point to the image and
call DetectText method

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.580
and print out the text.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:55.660
Now run the app.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.680
There you go.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.170
You just performed text
detection using the Vision API.

